    "description": "•\tLed a contractor team in upgrading a (MATLAB-based) visualization plotting program that allowed interface and comparison across a variety of tools in the Mission design directorate.\nDeveloped better process for simulation output visualization and plotting.  This reduced the time and effort required for data access and analysis, allowing more reliable analysis.\n•\tSimulation software input process development that allowed a single vehicle model to be used in a variety of Trajectory simulations of varying modeling detail, from Open-loop optimal trajectories, through Guidance controlled Ideal controller simulations, to closed-loop autopilot simulations modeling launch day winds, propellant sloshing and structural dynamic bending modes.\n•\tAnalyze trajectories for optimal System Performance.\nI updated the telemetry analysis tools and data during an antenna system upgrade, embedding the telemetry link margin tool within the trajectory simulation.\n•\tLead of the Control System analysis and design group through many rocket launch campaigns, while transitioning the group from San Diego to Denver operations.\n",
